## Summary

I've fixed the **"conversations.map is not a function"** error in both `messages.tsx` and `messages.ios.tsx` files.

### What was the problem?
The backend was returning `{"error":"Unauthorized"}` instead of an array of conversations. The code was trying to call `.map()` on this error object, which caused the crash.

### What I changed:
Added validation in the `loadConversations()` function to check if the API response is an array before setting the state:

```typescript
// Validate that data is an array before setting state
if (Array.isArray(data)) {
  setConversations(data);
} else {
  console.log('MessagesScreen: API returned non-array data:', data);
  setConversations([]);
}
```

Now the app will:
- ✅ Display conversations if the API returns an array
- ✅ Show the "No conversations yet" empty state if the API returns an error or non-array data
- ✅ Never crash with "conversations.map is not a function"

The error is now fixed and the app should work properly! The Messages tab will show an empty state until you set up authentication or the backend returns actual conversation data.

